      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/3/2/53",
      "text": [
        "تْ يَا رَسُولَ اَللَّهِ يَحْضُرُ اَلْأَضْحَى وَ لَيْسَ عِنْدِي ثَمَنُ اَلْأُضْحِيَّةِ فَأَسْتَقْرِضُ وَ أُضَحِّي فَقَالَ «اِسْتَقْرِضِي وَ ضَحِّي فَإِنَّهُ دَيْنٌ مَقْضِيٌّ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2191 - Umm Salamah, may Allah (swt) be pleased with her, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, and said:\n\"O Messenger of Allah (swt), the Day of Sacrifice is approaching, and I do not have the means to afford a sacrifice. Should I borrow and offer a sacrifice?\"\nHe (sw) replied: \"Borrow and offer a sacrifice, for it is a debt that will be repaid.\""
        ]
      }
